--TEST--
a keyed property access, `$object->$key`, may name any public property of the key's class, so it does not compile outside the places a restricted one allows, even when the key names a free property — `rule:packaging/a-restriction-limits-where-a-declaration-is-used`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// This file is the application. It is not in `App\Billing`.
autoload 'App' from './app';

var $ledger = new App\Billing\Ledger();
// `owner` is free, and a direct read compiles.
echo $ledger->owner, "\n";
// A key of `Ledger` may name `secret` too, so this read does not compile.
property<App\Billing\Ledger> $key = "owner" as property<App\Billing\Ledger>;
echo $ledger->$key, "\n";
// covers: tools:packages/restrictions-where-a-class-or-method-may-be-used
--FILE app/Billing/Ledger.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App\Billing;

final class Ledger
{
    public string $owner = "Shop";

    public string $secret = "1234";
}
--FILE package.toml--
[[restrict]]
use = 'App\Billing\Ledger::secret'
allow = ['App\Billing\*']
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0664]: `App\Billing\Ledger::secret` cannot be used here
   --> case.nvs:10:6
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
